-- title:
--   Splitting symmetric normalised 2-cocycles on a finite Hopf algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a perfect field of characteristic $p$, where $p$ is a prime, and let $R$ be a commutative ring carrying the structure of a Hopf algebra over $k$ which is finite-dimensional as a $k$-module, with counit $\varepsilon =$ `Coalgebra.counit` $: R \to k$. Let $c : R \to R \to k$ be a $k$-bilinear form (an element of $R \to_{\ell} R \to_{\ell} k$) satisfying: symmetry, $c(r)(s) = c(s)(r)$ for all $r,s$; the Hochschild cocycle identity $c(rs)(t) + c(r)(s)\,\varepsilon(t) = c(r)(st) + \varepsilon(r)\, c(s)(t)$ for all $r,s,t$; and normalisation $c(1)(s) = 0$ for all $s$. Assume further that there is a $k$-linear form $\ell : R \to k$ with $\ell(1) = 0$, with $\ell(r) = 0$ for every $r$ with $r^p = 0$, and with $c(r^{p-1})(r) = \ell(r)^p$ for every $r$ in the kernel of $\varepsilon$. The conclusion is that $c$ is a coboundary: there exists a $k$-linear form $u : R \to k$ such that $u(rs) = \varepsilon(r)\,u(s) + \varepsilon(s)\,u(r) + c(r)(s)$ for all $r, s \in R$.
--
--   Equivalently, the square-zero extension $R \oplus k e$ of $R$ determined by $c$, with $(r + \lambda e)(s + \mu e) = rs + (\varepsilon(r)\mu + \varepsilon(s)\lambda + c(r)(s))e$, admits a $k$-algebra section $r \mapsto r + u(r)e$ of the projection to $R$; the hypothesis on $\ell$ controls the $p$-th power map of that extension on the augmentation ideal. It is the algebraic input behind the lifting statement [`Deformation.exists_mem_wittHom_truncate_eq_of_forall_apply_coeff_last_eq_zero`](thm.html#Deformation.exists_mem_wittHom_truncate_eq_of_forall_apply_coeff_last_eq_zero), and its proof uses the faithful flatness criterion [`HopfAlgebra.faithfullyFlat_subalgebra_of_comul_mem_span_of_antipode_mem`](thm.html#HopfAlgebra.faithfullyFlat_subalgebra_of_comul_mem_span_of_antipode_mem) together with the dimension formula [`HopfAlgebra.finrank_quotient_span_pow_prime_eq_pow_finrank_cotangent`](thm.html#HopfAlgebra.finrank_quotient_span_pow_prime_eq_pow_finrank_cotangent) for the quotient of $R$ by the ideal generated by $p$-th powers of elements of the augmentation ideal.
